)\n    return out\n```\n\nWait — the \"discard node from all deps\" loop is O(V) per pop, making it O(V^2 + E). That's fine for typical use, but Kahn's with reverse adjacency is O(V + E log V)... Actually with a heap it's O((V+E) log V). The reverse adjacency approach:\n\n```python\ndef schedule(graph):\n    indeg = {}\n    dependents = {node: [] for node in graph}\n    for node, deps in graph.items():\n        for d in deps:\n            if d not in graph:\n                raise KeyError(d)\n        remaining = set(deps)\n        indeg[node] = len(remaining)\n        for d in remaining:\n            dependents[d].append(node)\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, careful with duplicate deps — using set dedupes. But remaining must be a new set so we don't mutate input lists (deps could be a list; iterating is fine, we never mutate). We only read deps. We don't mutate graph. Good.\n\nThe O(V^2) \"scan all deps each step\" is simpler; but the reverse-adjacency version is O(V + E + k log V), simplest asymptotically efficient. Let me do the heap + reverse adjacency.\n\nEdge cases:\n- Empty graph → return [].\n- Self-loop: dep == node → cycle → ValueError. With dedupe: remaining = {node}, indeg 1, never ready → ValueError. Good.\n- Duplicate deps: set() dedupes so indeg counts unique deps. When d processed, dependents[d] contains node once (since set iteration). Good.\n\nKeyError message: should raise KeyError for absent dependency. `raise KeyError(d)` — fine.\n\nLet me write the code and test.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The current implementation picks the first ready node in dict order (not lexicographically smallest), loops forever on cycles, and silently hangs on missing dependencies. I'll rewrite it with Kahn's algorithm using a heap for deterministic ordering, plus validation and cycle detection."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00144]","name":"write_file","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/flashbench_glm53_t04_4004122/t04/scheduler.py","content":"import heapq\n\n\ndef schedule(graph):\n    remaining = {}\n    dependents = {node: [] for node in graph}\n    for node, deps in graph.items():\n        unique = set(deps)\n        for dep in unique:\n            if dep not in graph:\n                raise KeyError(dep)\n            dependents[dep].append(node)\n        remaining[node] = unique\n\n    ready = [node for node, deps in remaining.items() if not deps]\n    heapq.heapify(ready)\n    out = []\n    while ready:\n        node = heapq.heappop(ready)\n        out.append(node)\n        for dependent in dependents[node]:\n            deps = remaining[dependent]\n            deps.discard(node)\n            if not deps:\n                heapq.heappush(ready, dependent)\n    if len(out) != len(graph):\n        raise ValueError(\"cycle detected in graph\")\n    return out\n"}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1789033595906,"messageId":"[UUID_00064]"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"[CALL_00144]","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The file /tmp/flashbench_glm53_t04_4004122/t04/scheduler.py has been updated successfully."}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"[UUID_00065]"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now run the public test and additional checks of my own.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll run the public test plus additional checks covering ordering, cycles, missing deps, non-mutation, and edge cases."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00145]","name":"shell_command","input":{"command":"python test_public.py && python - <<'EOF'\nfrom scheduler import schedule\n\n# lexicographic tie-breaking\nassert schedule({'a': [], 'b': [], 'c': []}) == ['a', 'b', 'c']\nassert schedule({'b': ['a'], 'a': []}) == ['a', 'b']\nassert schedule({'c': ['a','b'], 'b': [], 'a': []}) == ['a', 'b', 'c']\n\n# diamond: ready set tie-break\ng = {'d': ['b','c'], 'b': ['a'], 'c': ['a'], 'a': []}\nassert schedule(g) == ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd']\n\n# empty graph\nassert schedule({}) == []\n\n# sin